1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:39,190
Isasumi, Chilchuk?

2
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:41,950
Do you mind slowing down a bit?

3
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:44,650
The floor is full of gaps and it's hard to walk on.

4
00:01:45,590 --> 00:01:47,250
I didn't even notice.

5
00:01:48,170 --> 00:01:49,690
Let's take a little break.

6
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:53,130
Sure, whatever you say, Grandpa.

7
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:55,830
There's something I've been wondering.

8
00:01:56,410 --> 00:01:57,630
In these bodies,

9
00:01:58,190 --> 00:02:01,290
what's the gap between our actual age and the age we look?

10
00:02:02,110 --> 00:02:03,810
Laios, how old are you?

11
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:05,850
I'm 26 years old.

12
00:02:06,110 --> 00:02:07,530
Senshi, now that he's a dwarf,

13
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:09,330
how old does Laios look to you?

14
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:12,130
Hmm, I would say around 60.

15
00:02:12,670 --> 00:02:15,510
Dwarves live about two and a half times longer than tall men.

16
00:02:16,090 --> 00:02:18,390
So if I'm 26 as a tall man,

17
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:21,130
I'd be 65 as a dwarf.

18
00:02:21,270 --> 00:02:24,670
If our appearance adjusts our age relative to what race we are,

19
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:27,770
I'm kind of worried about our remaining lifespan.

20
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:30,970
Will we age at the rate we did before we transformed?

21
00:02:31,510 --> 00:02:33,650
Or will that change based on our new bodies?

22
00:02:34,970 --> 00:02:35,650
Hey, Marcel,

23
00:02:35,990 --> 00:02:38,070
if you think that doesn't affect you, you're wrong.

24
00:02:38,230 --> 00:02:39,570
Since you're a half foot now,

25
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:40,730
if it's the latter,

26
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:43,110
you'll only live till about 50 years old.

27
00:02:43,270 --> 00:02:44,750
In less than 40 years,

28
00:02:44,810 --> 00:02:47,290
you're gonna get all old and wrinkly and then die.

29
00:02:47,290 --> 00:02:53,430
A half foot's lifespan is that short?

30
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:54,730
I thought they lived to 100.

31
00:02:55,510 --> 00:02:57,270
There are some who live that long.

32
00:02:57,490 --> 00:02:58,710
But it's pretty rare.

33
00:03:04,450 --> 00:03:05,590
I'm only kidding.

34
00:03:06,430 --> 00:03:08,190
What I'm actually trying to say is,

35
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:09,290
if that was the case,

36
00:03:09,370 --> 00:03:11,190
then this mushroom is too good to be true.

37
00:03:11,430 --> 00:03:12,830
There are tons of people out there

38
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:15,010
who would pay a fortune to become another race,

39
00:03:15,010 --> 00:03:17,490
but I've never seen this mushroom in the markets.

40
00:03:17,890 --> 00:03:19,730
It means the change is only temporary

41
00:03:19,730 --> 00:03:22,410
or has some kind of awful side effect.

42
00:03:23,010 --> 00:03:24,210
Side effects, huh?

43
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:25,670
Possibly.

44
00:03:26,490 --> 00:03:28,710
I thought about using the changelings for something,

45
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:30,350
but I don't think it'd go well.

46
00:03:30,570 --> 00:03:31,770
What kind of something?

47
00:03:32,070 --> 00:03:33,990
You want to be a demi-human, don't you?

48
00:03:34,030 --> 00:03:35,290
No, that's not it.

49
00:03:35,830 --> 00:03:38,630
I was honestly thinking more in regards to Fallon.

50
00:03:38,870 --> 00:03:39,830
What about her?

51
00:03:40,190 --> 00:03:41,810
Now, this is all hypothetical,

52
00:03:41,810 --> 00:03:44,030
but what if everything worked out

53
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:45,590
and we defeated the Mad Mage?

54
00:03:46,050 --> 00:03:47,610
I've learned my lesson.

55
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:49,490
Fallon regains her sanity.

56
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:50,110
Huh?

57
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:52,190
What was I just doing?

58
00:03:52,370 --> 00:03:53,330
Fallon's back!

59
00:03:53,790 --> 00:03:55,310
We return to the surface.

60
00:03:55,450 --> 00:03:57,290
Man, that was really rough, wasn't it?

61
00:03:58,250 --> 00:03:59,690
She scares people.

62
00:04:00,630 --> 00:04:02,610
So, in that case,

63
00:04:02,670 --> 00:04:04,910
having a dragon's lower half would be a problem.

64
00:04:05,190 --> 00:04:06,090
Hold on.

65
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:07,810
Let's hear what he has to say.

66
00:04:07,810 --> 00:04:11,170
I thought about hiding that part by putting her in a hole.

67
00:04:11,390 --> 00:04:12,330
What can I get to?

68
00:04:12,530 --> 00:04:12,930
However,

69
00:04:13,930 --> 00:04:16,310
a large monster can't survive in a human town

70
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:17,670
with how thin the mana is.

71
00:04:18,390 --> 00:04:21,050
Like how a fish can't survive outside of water,

72
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:24,410
Fallon might not be able to live among humans anymore.

73
00:04:25,430 --> 00:04:26,030
Unless...

74
00:04:26,030 --> 00:04:28,150
We use those mushrooms.

75
00:04:28,710 --> 00:04:29,830
With the changelings,

76
00:04:30,150 --> 00:04:31,750
we could change her lower half

77
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:33,130
into another type of dragon

78
00:04:33,130 --> 00:04:34,090
that's smaller.

79
00:04:34,090 --> 00:04:35,470
And that way,

80
00:04:35,830 --> 00:04:38,070
Fallon could live in town after all!

81
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:39,150
What?

82
00:04:39,470 --> 00:04:41,250
He's so stupidly optimistic.

83
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:41,850
Miss!

84
00:04:42,110 --> 00:04:42,430
Miss!

85
00:04:42,910 --> 00:04:43,270
Though,

86
00:04:43,570 --> 00:04:46,470
I won't deny wanting to change into something else, too.

87
00:04:46,970 --> 00:04:48,910
Tall men don't have any kind of special trait,

88
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:50,070
which makes us plain.

89
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:50,810
Jilchuk,

90
00:04:51,010 --> 00:04:52,670
do you hear something strange?

91
00:04:52,870 --> 00:04:53,630
Oh, uh,

92
00:04:53,810 --> 00:04:55,890
do you think it's the dwarven relic or something?

93
00:04:56,370 --> 00:04:56,890
No,

94
00:04:57,090 --> 00:04:59,650
it's like stones scraping against each other.

95
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:01,370
From what I can tell,

96
00:05:01,370 --> 00:05:03,370
it actually sounds like it's getting closer.

97
00:05:03,370 --> 00:05:06,630
This is bad!

98
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:08,810
The gargoyles found us!

99
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:10,090
You idiot!

100
00:05:10,210 --> 00:05:11,970
Did you really not shut the door all the way?

101
00:05:12,230 --> 00:05:14,170
We need to hurry and get out of here

102
00:05:14,170 --> 00:05:16,070
before they catch up to us!

103
00:05:16,890 --> 00:05:18,590
They're just gonna keep chasing us

104
00:05:18,590 --> 00:05:19,490
unless we do something.

105
00:05:20,190 --> 00:05:22,210
Let's set up an ambush and take them down.

106
00:05:23,270 --> 00:05:24,630
But, Laios...

107
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:25,610
I'll draw them to me.

108
00:05:26,110 --> 00:05:26,530
Jilchuk,

109
00:05:26,710 --> 00:05:27,290
get the pan!

110
00:05:27,510 --> 00:05:28,030
Izutsumi,

111
00:05:28,170 --> 00:05:28,930
attack from behind!

112
00:05:29,410 --> 00:05:29,750
Senji,

113
00:05:29,870 --> 00:05:30,570
wait for an opening.

114
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:31,230
Marcel,

115
00:05:31,470 --> 00:05:32,290
where are they?

116
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:33,550
I told you!

117
00:05:33,950 --> 00:05:35,150
They're right there!

118
00:05:38,330 --> 00:05:38,930
Laios!

119
00:05:41,610 --> 00:05:42,210
Dammit!

120
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:44,110
Watch out, everyone!

121
00:05:50,450 --> 00:05:51,730
Now do you understand

122
00:05:51,730 --> 00:05:52,830
why I quickly run off

123
00:05:52,830 --> 00:05:53,990
and find a place to hide?

124
00:05:53,990 --> 00:05:55,970
Don't stand around people's legs!

125
00:05:56,030 --> 00:05:57,270
You say that, but...

126
00:05:57,270 --> 00:05:59,710
You're clumsy no matter what body you're in, huh?

127
00:05:59,930 --> 00:06:00,670
This way!

128
00:06:04,850 --> 00:06:06,650
Where did this smoke come from?

129
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:09,010
Did you cast something?

130
00:06:10,010 --> 00:06:11,110
Are you two hurt?

131
00:06:11,550 --> 00:06:12,510
No, we're fine.

132
00:06:12,650 --> 00:06:14,070
It went right between our arms.

133
00:06:14,450 --> 00:06:14,930
Good.

134
00:06:15,610 --> 00:06:17,110
You mind grabbing Kensuke for me?

135
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:17,490
Sure.

136
00:06:17,490 --> 00:06:22,670
Has it always looked like this?

137
00:06:22,870 --> 00:06:23,270
No.

138
00:06:23,730 --> 00:06:25,510
How and when did it change, then?

139
00:06:25,950 --> 00:06:28,090
You think that maybe the smoke we saw

140
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:30,730
was actually changeling spores?

141
00:06:31,290 --> 00:06:32,350
But, hang on.

142
00:06:32,590 --> 00:06:34,970
There wasn't a mushroom ring anywhere near here.

143
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:37,310
Our arms were a ring when it passed through them.

144
00:06:38,630 --> 00:06:40,490
Wait, so that means...

145
00:06:40,490 --> 00:06:48,470
Quit buzzing around, dammit!

146
00:06:48,770 --> 00:06:49,510
You guys!

147
00:06:49,810 --> 00:06:50,810
Grab each other's hands

148
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:52,290
and make a circle right now!

149
00:06:52,410 --> 00:06:54,130
Think before you open your mouth for once!

150
00:06:54,150 --> 00:06:55,110
Just trust me, okay?

151
00:06:58,370 --> 00:06:58,810
Well?

152
00:06:59,190 --> 00:07:00,350
What do we do now?

153
00:07:00,450 --> 00:07:01,150
Is this it?

154
00:07:01,410 --> 00:07:02,690
We're gonna have the gargoyle

155
00:07:02,690 --> 00:07:03,790
pass through our arms.

156
00:07:04,130 --> 00:07:05,470
If my theory is correct,

157
00:07:05,470 --> 00:07:06,610
then the gargoyle

158
00:07:06,610 --> 00:07:08,290
should change into something else!

159
00:07:08,290 --> 00:07:11,270
All right, it's time!

160
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:12,990
The wall's in that direction!

161
00:07:13,230 --> 00:07:13,870
Come this way!

162
00:07:13,870 --> 00:07:14,190
Hey!

163
00:07:14,430 --> 00:07:14,950
Stop!

164
00:07:15,190 --> 00:07:17,010
You're hurting me!

165
00:07:20,890 --> 00:07:21,970
Oh, no!

166
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:34,810
It can't fly away anymore!

167
00:07:34,970 --> 00:07:35,450
Come on!

168
00:07:35,570 --> 00:07:36,410
Let's surround it!

169
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:46,470
We did it!

170
00:07:46,970 --> 00:07:47,710
Where'd it go?

171
00:07:48,330 --> 00:07:48,790
Look!

172
00:07:52,130 --> 00:07:53,730
This is the gargoyle?

173
00:07:54,190 --> 00:07:55,570
It really did change.

174
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:56,850
I see.

175
00:07:57,110 --> 00:07:58,330
It works like this, too.

176
00:07:58,930 --> 00:07:59,870
So non-living,

177
00:08:00,030 --> 00:08:01,370
things transform faster!

178
00:08:01,370 --> 00:08:03,090
Glyos!

179
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:04,090
Are you okay?

180
00:08:04,510 --> 00:08:05,450
My head hurts,

181
00:08:05,550 --> 00:08:06,250
but I'm fine.

182
00:08:06,930 --> 00:08:07,650
Dwarves' bodies

183
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:08,950
are as tough as they say.

184
00:08:12,410 --> 00:08:13,390
Doesn't seem like

185
00:08:13,390 --> 00:08:14,590
it's gonna come down here.

186
00:08:14,990 --> 00:08:15,910
How are we supposed

187
00:08:15,910 --> 00:08:16,790
to get it to pass

188
00:08:16,790 --> 00:08:17,650
through our arms?

189
00:08:22,450 --> 00:08:22,850
Marcil?

190
00:08:23,090 --> 00:08:23,390
Yeah?

191
00:08:23,490 --> 00:08:24,370
What if we...

192
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:29,410
It should work.

193
00:08:29,490 --> 00:08:30,050
What should...

194
00:08:30,050 --> 00:08:30,710
Let's do it!

195
00:08:30,910 --> 00:08:31,170
Right.

196
00:08:32,270 --> 00:08:33,030
We're gonna bring

197
00:08:33,030 --> 00:08:34,370
ourselves closer to it

198
00:08:34,370 --> 00:08:36,310
and get it to attack us!

199
00:08:36,490 --> 00:08:37,110
Keep in rhythm

200
00:08:37,110 --> 00:08:38,330
so we run and sink!

201
00:08:38,710 --> 00:08:39,450
Let's go!

202
00:08:40,130 --> 00:08:40,550
One!

203
00:08:40,550 --> 00:08:41,550
Two!

204
00:08:41,550 --> 00:08:41,990
One!

205
00:08:41,990 --> 00:08:42,550
Two!

206
00:08:42,550 --> 00:08:42,790
One!

207
00:08:43,050 --> 00:08:43,690
Two!

208
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:44,490
One!

209
00:08:44,490 --> 00:08:44,790
One!

210
00:08:45,170 --> 00:08:45,710
Two!

211
00:08:46,250 --> 00:08:47,930
One and two and one

212
00:08:47,930 --> 00:08:49,170
and two and one

213
00:08:49,170 --> 00:08:50,170
and two and...

214
00:08:50,170 --> 00:08:53,270
It's making its move!

215
00:08:53,390 --> 00:08:54,350
You ready to do this?

216
00:08:54,430 --> 00:08:54,770
Ready!

217
00:08:55,050 --> 00:08:55,990
Ready for what?

218
00:08:56,010 --> 00:08:57,670
Ready and...

219
00:08:57,670 --> 00:08:59,070
Take to the sky, Marcil!

220
00:08:59,070 --> 00:08:59,350
Marcil!

221
00:09:04,350 --> 00:09:05,070
Ah!

222
00:09:13,690 --> 00:09:15,650
Good riddance.

223
00:09:17,090 --> 00:09:18,830
It's kind of anticlimactic,

224
00:09:19,370 --> 00:09:20,390
but if you wash off

225
00:09:20,390 --> 00:09:21,950
the spores stuck to your body,

226
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:23,210
you'll go back to normal.

227
00:09:24,130 --> 00:09:25,470
Can you please not?

228
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:26,570
All it is is water,

229
00:09:26,710 --> 00:09:27,330
so it's fine.

230
00:09:27,770 --> 00:09:28,910
Gotta rinse the spores

231
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:29,530
off thoroughly.

232
00:09:30,170 --> 00:09:30,790
We're basically

233
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:32,190
the mushroom seedbed

234
00:09:32,190 --> 00:09:32,710
right now.

235
00:09:33,850 --> 00:09:35,670
I think I finally understand

236
00:09:35,670 --> 00:09:36,550
why the mushrooms

237
00:09:36,550 --> 00:09:37,870
behave the way they do.

238
00:09:39,030 --> 00:09:40,110
An animal steps

239
00:09:40,110 --> 00:09:41,230
into a changeling ring

240
00:09:41,230 --> 00:09:42,270
and transforms.

241
00:09:42,270 --> 00:09:44,070
They get shunned

242
00:09:44,070 --> 00:09:44,890
by their kind,

243
00:09:45,130 --> 00:09:46,290
then they die,

244
00:09:46,570 --> 00:09:47,310
and eventually

245
00:09:47,310 --> 00:09:48,350
become new changelings.

246
00:09:49,390 --> 00:09:50,390
What an awful

247
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:51,210
side effect.

248
00:09:51,650 --> 00:09:53,310
Since we're not gargoyles,

249
00:09:53,370 --> 00:09:54,450
it's gonna take some time

250
00:09:54,450 --> 00:09:55,750
to go back to how we were.

251
00:09:56,210 --> 00:09:57,030
Why don't we prepare

252
00:09:57,030 --> 00:09:58,170
a meal while we wait?

253
00:09:59,210 --> 00:10:00,190
Very well.

254
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:04,130
Kensuke,

255
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:05,810
it's hard to believe

256
00:10:05,810 --> 00:10:07,230
that this is you now.

257
00:10:08,350 --> 00:10:09,910
Maybe it's a bit of a stretch

258
00:10:09,910 --> 00:10:10,870
to think the mushrooms

259
00:10:10,870 --> 00:10:12,050
were the cause of this.

260
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:14,110
Will washing you

261
00:10:14,110 --> 00:10:15,150
change you back?

262
00:10:18,430 --> 00:10:19,410
What's on the menu?

263
00:10:19,950 --> 00:10:21,490
We have some leftover dumplings,

264
00:10:21,650 --> 00:10:22,870
so I'll be boiling those.

265
00:10:23,190 --> 00:10:23,650
Really?

266
00:10:23,810 --> 00:10:24,250
Again?

267
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,210
Is there a problem with that?

268
00:10:26,730 --> 00:10:27,190
Nah,

269
00:10:27,370 --> 00:10:28,610
I'm just kind of sick of them.

270
00:10:29,730 --> 00:10:30,490
Sick of them?

271
00:10:30,510 --> 00:10:31,950
Wish I could be that carefree.

272
00:10:33,850 --> 00:10:35,570
Let's cook them another way.

273
00:10:36,950 --> 00:10:38,870
Heat some oil in a frying pan,

274
00:10:38,870 --> 00:10:41,030
then gently put the dumplings in.

275
00:10:42,090 --> 00:10:43,210
Oh, shit.

276
00:10:44,030 --> 00:10:45,330
When golden brown,

277
00:10:45,450 --> 00:10:46,430
remove the dumplings

278
00:10:46,430 --> 00:10:48,050
and blot the excess oil.

279
00:10:48,670 --> 00:10:49,790
On top of Izutsumi

280
00:10:49,790 --> 00:10:51,010
having a small appetite,

281
00:10:51,430 --> 00:10:52,350
she won't eat anything

282
00:10:52,350 --> 00:10:53,230
she doesn't like.

283
00:10:53,850 --> 00:10:54,790
So it's important

284
00:10:54,790 --> 00:10:56,150
I take extra care

285
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:57,170
to make sure

286
00:10:57,170 --> 00:10:58,210
she eats her fill.

287
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:02,150
Tell me,

288
00:11:02,250 --> 00:11:03,310
what do you think?

289
00:11:03,310 --> 00:11:04,970
You just fried them.

290
00:11:05,970 --> 00:11:07,010
Could you not?

291
00:11:07,970 --> 00:11:08,230
Huh?

292
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:13,230
What if...

293
00:11:13,230 --> 00:11:20,830
Oh, it changed its shape.

